{{also|Apsis|āpsis}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|apsis}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἁψίς||arch, vault}}. See also {{m|en|apse}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|apsides}}

# {{label|en|architecture}} A [[recess]] or [[projection]], with a [[dome]] or [[vault]], at the [[east]] end of a [[church]]; an [[apse]].
# {{label|en|astronomy}} Either of the [[point]]s in the [[elliptical]] [[orbit]] of a [[planet]] or [[comet]] where it is [[closest]] or [[furthest]] from the [[sun]]; [[perihelion]] or [[aphelion]]; an [[apside]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|periapsis}}
* {{l|en|apoapsis}}

